-- title:
--   Chart factorisation of the generic point avoids [0:1:0]
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative integral domain and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$ which is elliptic (so its discriminant is a unit). Write $E = \mathrm{Proj}$ of the grading obtained by pushing the homogeneous grading of $R[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ forward along the quotient by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of `W.toProjective`, and let $\pi : E \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be the structure morphism `projModelStrCR`, namely `Proj.toSpecZero` followed by the map induced by $R \to$ (degree-zero part). Smoothness of $\pi$, geometric integrality of $\pi$ (via the base-change isomorphisms identifying pullbacks of $E$ with projective models over fields), and integrality of $E$ are installed inline, and the function field $K = K(E)$ is given the $R$-algebra structure coming from the composite of the generic-point morphism $\operatorname{Spec} K \to E$ with $\pi$; the non-vanishing of the image of $W.\Delta$ in $K$ is recorded inline and the conclusion does not refer to it. The assertion is that there exist an index $i \in \{0,1,2\}$ and an $R$-algebra homomorphism $\psi$ from the degree-zero homogeneous localisation `Away` of the graded quotient ring at the class of $X_i$ into $K$ such that the morphism `fromSpecStalk` at the generic point of $E$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\psi)$ followed by the $i$-th map of the standard affine open cover of $E$, and such that the projective point class of the triple $k \mapsto \psi(\mathrm{gen}\,i\,k)$ over $K$ differs from the class of $(0,1,0)$.
--
--   This is the statement that the generic point of the projective Weierstrass model, read through a standard affine chart, is not the point at infinity; it is the geometric input to [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_genericPoint_ne_zero`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_genericPoint_ne_zero) and to the independence statement [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_triple_projections_chartFactor_pointClass_indep`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_triple_projections_chartFactor_pointClass_indep) for the comparison between the scheme-theoretic model and the Weierstrass group law on $K(E)$-points.
